<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  Robot-side Fast DDS profile: UDP ONLY, no interface whitelist.

  WHY
  Fast DDS prefers shared memory between participants on the same host. On this Jetson the
  SHM transport repeatedly fails to reuse its port segments:
      [RTPS_TRANSPORT_SHM Error] Failed init_port fastrtps_port7411:
          open_and_lock_file failed -> Function open_port_internal
  That is not cosmetic. With it, every controller_manager becomes unreachable and the whole
  ROS graph on this machine goes dark - stacks running, control nodes alive, and
  `recover.py - -check` reporting "controller_manager not reachable" for both arms and the
  base. Deleting /dev/shm/fastrtps_* clears it only until the segments accumulate again.
  Removing the SHM transport removes the failure mode. Localhost then uses UDP, exactly
  like the cross-host path that has always worked.

  EDITED 2026-08-27:
  * receiverBufferSize -> receiveBufferSize. The old name is not a valid element, so Fast
    DDS 2.6 rejected the WHOLE profile at parse time (XMLPARSER errors at every node start)
    and every node silently fell back to default transports - SHM included, the exact
    failure this file exists to prevent. Symptom on 2026-08-27: spawner service replies
    lost ("sequence size exceeds remaining buffer"), spawner retry then died on
    "controller already loaded".
  * interfaceWhiteList (172.16.1.9 + lo) REMOVED. It pinned all DDS to the direct 2.5GbE
    link to ebimHP, but that link is no longer cabled: eno1 carrier=0 here and ebimHP has
    no 172.16.1.x address on any interface. Pinning a transport to a missing address makes
    every topic silently undiscoverable (the stale-address trap documented in
    record_bag.bash). Because of the parse failure above, the whitelist was never actually
    in effect anyway.
  Previous version preserved as ~/fastdds_udp_only.xml.bak-parseerror.
-->
<dds>
  <profiles xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
    <transport_descriptors>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>udp_all_ifaces</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
        <sendBufferSize>12582912</sendBufferSize>
        <receiveBufferSize>12582912</receiveBufferSize>
        <maxMessageSize>1400</maxMessageSize>
      </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>
    <participant profile_name="robot_udp_only" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>udp_all_ifaces</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      </rtps>
    </participant>
  </profiles>
</dds>
